{
  "_meta": {
    "name": "FormuSense process & category library",
    "version": "1.0",
    "note": "Each category declares formulation slots (what kind of ingredient goes where and roughly how much), a unit-operation sequence and the process parameters the physics engine consumes. A category may also declare pack_unit, the unit its pack size is stated in: ml for a product sold by volume (a drink), g otherwise. typical_unit_weight_g is then the mass the models work in, and for a density near 1 g/ml the two numbers are the same. Parameter ids used by the engine: bake_temp_c, bake_time_min, water_added_pct, sheet_thickness_mm, cook_temp_c, cook_time_min, hot_fill_temp_c, blend_time_min, roast_temp_c, barrel_temp_c, screw_speed_rpm, feed_moisture_pct, dryer_temp_c, dryer_time_min, syrup_temp_c, cooling_temp_c, hydration_temp_c, heat_treat_temp_c, hold_time_s, fill_temp_c."
